mantle rm288
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_roald_greyham
title the diagonal walker
fits stage=adult|old
prefers role=civilian
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=frank piety=devout drive=steady
quirk imagines_a_draughts_board_on_each_stair
likes warm_bread draughts market_bustle misty_dawns
dislikes waiting early_bells
fears leaving_no_clear_move_for_a_friend
hopes to_play_a_game_on_a_quiet_landing
topics pastimes +0.4 faith +0.3 day +0.2 food +0.2
styles comfort=practical gossip=quiet refuse=flat tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# finds the diagonal between two stair treads and considers every draughts move an occasion for plain dealing.

words
oath! = Square my stride | By the last free corner
saying! = No prize for rushing past your turn | A good move leaves a landing
board = my little chequerboard | a board of painted squares
piece = a smooth white counter | a chip of black horn
move = a diagonal pace | my sideways advance
steam = a twist of steam | a curl of warm air
cloth = a close-woven towel | my striped cloth
crust = the warm heel | a crust still soft within
bustle = the babble of stalls | a whole street calling
mist = a mist-white corner | the pale morning wall
bell = the waking clang | a hard early stroke
bench = a plain oak bench | a seat with room beside me
step = the wide tread | a short cross step
square = an empty dark square | the uncovered corner

any
opinion church for 2 : My own prayers fit under the same roof as a cold stranger. That's a properly useful roof.
opinion dole for 3 : When my cupboard was nothing but wood I got hot food without giving up my last coin.
opinion drink against 1 : A wolf should be able to remember a promise until morning. I've seen a cup undo that.
opinion houses against 2 : They can find room for a bench longer than two carts and no space to fit me on it.
opinion merchants against 3 : I work to bring home a hot heel and sometimes get the smell alone.

grown
line greet [pair.band=strangers] : Here's your place across from me. | Welcome. I'll sit square.
line greet [self.working=yes] : Stay by the free corner. | Speak plainly above the work.
line greet [here.time=dawn] : Pale board to begin the morning. | You have the first daylight move.
line greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Evening. My bench has a spare end. | Short light, clear hearing.
line kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : I'll move over for kin. | Ah, my own family across the board.
line again.open : Back on my diagonal again. | The second meeting's ours.
line greet.return : Welcome. I can wait one turn. | I'll hear the full move.
line greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : You can keep the warm corner. | Glad of a familiar voice beside me.
line greet.return [self.working=yes] : I've a clean moment between jobs. | Tell me before the next turn.
line greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Stay in the little square of lamplight. | Evening. Set your feet here.
line farewell : Keep a landing in reach. | Safe play all your way back.
line farewell.return : Leave room for a good return. | I'll mind this corner.
line farewell.return [here.time=night] : Look for the next lamp before turning. | A quiet rest when you reach home.
line react.news : Make the account plain. | Which part came to you clean?
line react.news.new : New square to my eyes. | I hadn't heard that move.
line react.news.known : That piece has crossed my board. | I've already considered that word.
line react.news.doubt : I'd see the rest of the position first. | A move like that wants a second look.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Hard news reaches both sides equally. | I'll sit across from you in silence.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : A glad turn for once. | I'd make room for more word like that.
line ask.how : How's your side of the board? | Can you find an easy move today?
line answer.how : Making quiet progress with both feet. | Still plenty to occupy one turn.
line decline : I'd sooner finish the task on my bench. | I need a quieter corner than that today.
line accept_decline : Clear refusal. I can honour it. | Then your turn stands.
line thank : I'll keep a corner open for you. | That gives my feet a rest.
line sympathise : You needn't find a winning move straight off. | Hold steady. I'll keep the bench.
line reassure : A pause is a proper move sometimes. | Plenty of room to consider it.
line preclose : I'll leave my counter here. | Time to rest these jumping feet.

scene stair
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A stair looks like half a draughts board from below.
b : Which half? | Do you play as you go?
a : The dark squares come in pairs where the light misses the rail. | I jump the middle tread if the landing's clear.

scene bath
when topic=work self.job=none self.working=yes self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# the best bench is the one with a clear way off.
b : Not the warmest? | Why that bench?
a : A wolf getting to hot water ought to have one free elbow. | A slippery foot and a crowded corner are poor company.

scene draughts
when topic=pastimes self.likes=draughts
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I won't touch a counter until I've said its next square in my head.
b : To avoid mistakes? | What do you call the squares?
a : To avoid nudging it backwards when the mistake shows up. | Near corner, far wall, quiet centre. Names enough for me.

scene prayer
when topic=faith self.piety=devout
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When I'm kept waiting, I pray for enough patience to last me.
b : Does the prayer work? | Why patience in particular?
a : Sometimes I get exercise for it straightaway. | I can usually supply my own impatience.

scene bread
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I buy a loaf warm enough to soften the crust beside it.
b : How can you tell? | Doesn't it get squashed?
a : Give the wrapping time. The warmest part shines through. | I carry it on my palm. A loaf deserves a little ceremony.

scene market
when topic=day self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I enjoy a market most where two rows meet.
b : Twice the noise? | Not too crowded?
a : Twice the different accents, which is better. | I can change direction without holding up a whole row.

scene mist
when topic=weather self.likes=misty_dawns
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A misty dawn gives every street just one square ahead.
b : Is that enough? | Do you get lost?
a : Enough for a careful step. I like being reminded. | My toes know where the kerb is before I see it.

scene bells
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The first bell takes my sleep without asking.
b : Do you rise then? | What do you wish it would do?
a : Well awake by then, even with my nose tucked under a paw. | Begin with one civil knock before emptying the whole tower.

scene wait
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=waiting
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Waiting's hardest with the finish hidden.
b : A long queue? | How do you keep occupied?
a : A closed door with no noise coming out is worse. | I play the opening of a quiet game on my palm.

scene friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd clear the whole board to sit beside #self.friend#.
b : Even near the end? | Do you remember the position?
a : That'd be a dearer gift, which is all to the good. | I usually do. There's no hurry to put it back.

scene thin
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A thin wage won't buy another dark square to jump to.
b : No way out? | What about a cheaper loaf?
a : There are usually moves. Just fewer after the bread's bought. | Less of it left when the money's spent.

scene chapel
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep a chapel seat clear beside me.
b : For your elbows? | At the end?
a : For the wolf that came last through the door. | Halfway down. A newcomer needn't stand where every head turns.

scene steam
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A little steam makes my old cuts show pale.
b : Do they hurt? | Every one of them?
a : No. It's just a small map under the fur. | Just the ones my fur grows round instead of over.

scene town
when topic=home self.quarter=sump
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In the Sump the tidy route is rarely the straight one.
b : Where do you turn? | What makes it tidy?
a : Where a pair of neighbours can pass abreast of a parcel. | Finishing at the door without stepping on another tail.

scene charcoal
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I still like the hush of a hearth settling to coals.
b : From a hearth? | What can you hear then?
a : Any hearth. I needn't own it to enjoy that moment. | The slow settling before the ash gives way.

scene stranger
when topic=newcomer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd play a newcomer without asking where the journey began.
b : To spare the traveller? | How would you greet a stranger?
a : To enjoy a game without deciding who's on which side of town. | Put the counters out. Offer the first move.

scene plain
when topic=gossip
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like my talk as visible as a board under a lamp.
b : No secrets at all? | What's a hidden move?
a : Plenty. I just keep them out of other wolves' business. | Repeating something softly and hoping the blame goes past you.

scene dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I dreamt the stairs had black and white treads that kept changing places.
b : Could you get anywhere? | Any other players?
a : Straight into the wall. The board was turned on its side. | My own feet had opposing ideas.

story steamboard [topic=pastimes]
  : I drew a draughts board with my finger on a steamed window. The first half came out beautifully, the second began running into my palm.
  : Before my imaginary counters were in place the warm squares had gone. It was the briefest game I've ever played.
  b : Who won?
  : The window. I wiped it and got enough light to find my real board.

story staircoin [topic=memories]
  : I dropped a counter on a stair and watched it hop sideways down three treads. I hopped down sideways after it.
  : At the bottom it slipped under the board where I couldn't reach. I could just see the white edge.
  b : Did you lose it there?
  : I came back with a strip of bread wrapper and fished it out. I've never taken that corner for granted since.

story marketheel [topic=food]
  : A loaf I carried under my arm warmed my counters so well that my fingers recognised the wooden counters with my eyes shut.
  : The horn stayed cool. The wood took a little warm breath from the crust and gave it back into my palm.
  b : Did that help your game?
  : It helped remind me to eat before sitting down to one.

rule @aside1
when concept=bark self.job=none self.working=yes
does aside
cooldown 6h
say Dry seat and a free way round. | Straighten that towel before someone steps on it.

rule @aside2
when concept=bark self.likes=draughts
does aside
cooldown 7h
say Black on the diagonal. White bides awhile. | No jump through an occupied landing.

rule @aside3
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One bell would have served. | Bright One lend the next sound a softer edge.

rule @aside4
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 9h
say A little heat still in the middle. | Fold the wrapping over the warm heel.

dlg resident.hub : Take the corner that suits you. I like folk to see who they're talking with.
dlg resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you know the way across my board.
dlg resident.job [self.job=none self.working=yes self.workplace] : There are benches and towels to see to at #self.workplace#. A dry seat's a small kindness.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : A clear word has reached me. #world.news#
dlg resident.bye : Keep an open square ahead as you go.

graft resident.hub
choice Show me the draughts board on a stair. -> walk_board
node walk_board
say Start against the rail. Look up one tread and a little to the side. That's your diagonal. When there's nobody coming down, go two at a time.
free
choice What if somebody is coming down? -> walk_wait
choice I see the dark squares now. -> hub
node walk_wait
say Then the best move I can make is to stand still. Disliking a wait doesn't entitle me to somebody else's half of a stair.
choice A fair rule. -> hub
choice I'll take my turn outside. -> bye
